# Fixtures — no secrets

Never add realistic credentials, tokens, webhook URLs, connection strings, or cloud keys to tests, testdata, or examples.

Use obviously fake values only, for example:

- `REDACTED_TEST_VALUE`
- `https://example.test/hook`
- `owner/repo` placeholders without real tokens
- `AKIA` / `ghp_` / Slack `hooks.slack.com` style strings that look real → **forbidden** even in fixtures

Prefer rewriting history-sensitive false positives out of the branch before push (GitGuardian scans PR commits).

If a test needs “secret-shaped” input, use a clearly invalid synthetic pattern documented in the test name or comment.
